course: dictionary
lesson: 12781
title: Fizzy or full of life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Effervescent is an adjective, a word that describes a noun. It has two meanings: for a liquid, it means giving off bubbles of gas, so it is fizzy; for a person, it means lively, cheerful and full of energy.
explain: «The effervescent lemonade bubbled up the sides of the glass.» The clue is bubbled: the drink is giving off gas bubbles, so effervescent means fizzy here.
explain: «Her effervescent personality made the whole class smile.» The clue is made the class smile: she is bubbly and full of energy, so effervescent describes her character.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in fizzy for a drink or lively for a person. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Effervescent means giving off bubbles of gas, or fizzy, when it describes a liquid.
fact: Effervescent also describes a person who is lively, cheerful and full of energy.
fact: In science, «an effervescent tablet» fizzes when you drop it into water.
fact: Fizzy is the closest synonym for a liquid; bubbly or lively can fit a person.
exercise: «The effervescent drink fizzed in the glass.» What does effervescent mean here? | *Giving off bubbles of gas | Dark and thick | Sweet and sticky | Very cold and frozen
exercise: «Mia is so effervescent that everyone wants to sit by her.» What does effervescent mean here? | Tired and sleepy | Angry and loud | Quiet and shy | *Lively and full of energy
exercise: Which word could replace effervescent when it describes a fizzy drink? | Cold | *Fizzy | Still | Heavy
test: «The effervescent tablet dropped into the water and fizzed loudly.» What does effervescent mean here? | Hard as a rock | Sour and bitter | Smelly and old | *Giving off bubbles of gas as it fizzes
test: «Our effervescent class captain led every game with a big smile.» Which meaning fits? | *Lively, cheerful and full of energy | Very heavy | Sad and tired | Giving off bubbles of gas
exam: Which sentence uses effervescent to describe a person, not a drink? | The effervescent tablet dropped in the cup | The effervescent water was cloudy | *The effervescent girl danced all afternoon | The effervescent soda was cold
